// HZM coop - SHARED MULTIPLAYER SETUP (host game setup, one screen shared by every HZM MP mode). MP-OWNED
// menu (coop_mp* name, in MP_MANIFEST), so it may name the MP cvars coop_mpMode / coop_mpPreset and the MP
// launch cfg tree ui/coop_mpmenu/. The menu id STAYS "coop_mpmenu" on purpose: ui/multiplayerstart.urc is a
// COOP-classified file and check_mp_isolation clause 7 lets a coop file name exactly ONE coop_mp* token - the
// literal "coop_mpmenu" - so that screen reaches this one and no other by name. Loaded automatically by the
// engine ui/*.urc sweep (cl_ui.cpp CL_InitializeUI). INERT in coop: never pushed there, and its controls only
// set MP-owned coop_mp* / ui_mp* cvars.
//
// FLOW: on the Select Game Type screen each HZM mode button execs ui/coop_mpmenu/start_<mode>.cfg, which sets
// coop_mpMode, seeds a default map, sets exactly one launch-gametype flag ui_mpGt1/ui_mpGt2/ui_mpGt4 (the mode's
// g_gametype: gungame=1 FFA, koth/lms/freezetag/push=2, snd=4 objective), then pushes THIS menu. Here the host
// sees the mode (readout), picks a weapon preset, opens HOST RULES (bots + Hardcore), picks a map, and Starts.
//
// SELECTED-STATE READOUTS: enabledcvar tests integer truthiness only (uiwidget.cpp isEnabled) and cannot gate on
// a STRING cvar value, so the mode/preset readouts use linkcvar + linkstring (string equality, uilabel.cpp
// FindLinkString) and fall back to their title before any pick.
//
// START launches per mode WITHOUT vstr (isolation clause 18 - the MP UI is client-origin and a server-stuffed
// vstr is filtered) and WITHOUT $-substitution (which does not expand a dynamically-set cvar): three START
// buttons share one rect, each gated by an integer flag ui_mpGt1/2/4 so exactly one shows, and each execs the
// matching ui/coop_mpmenu/launch_gt<n>.cfg, which seeds the MP server cvars and calls ui_startdmmap <n>
// (cl_ui.cpp UI_StartDMMap_f: arg 1 = g_gametype, then `map <ui_dmmap>`). coop_mpMode was already set by the mode
// button and persists to the map load, where mp.scr reads it. A level load wipes level vars, so nothing follows
// anyone into coop.
//
// This file names ONLY coop_mp* / ui_mp* / ui_dmmap and the ui/coop_mpmenu/ cfg tree - never a coop_* gameplay
// cvar, never coop_lo* / ui/loadout / a coop_mod path, never the coop_loadout menu. The three loadout-chooser
// buttons that used to live here (Allied/Axis/coop armory opens) were REMOVED (they move to the lobby closet in a
// separate pass); no ui/loadout/open.cfg or coop_mpa_/coop_mpx_ armory open remains here.
//
// URC conventions: each resource field on its own line (single-line blocks silently drop); colour fills for
// panels, never raw-image shaders (bug-menu-shader-label-invisible); canvas stays 640x480 (bug-1365); ASCII,
// no em-dash. Declaration order is draw + hit order.
menu "coop_mpmenu" 640 480 NONE 1
borderstyle NONE
bgcolor 0 0 0 0
align centerx centery
virtualres 1
fullscreen 0

direction from_top 0

